                         Contributing to the repository

Thank you for your interest in contributing.

Before submitting a contribution, read the `LICENSE` in every project
directory that the change modifies. Each project is separately licensed.
Unless the Project Owner has explicitly designated a license for it, do not
submit changes to repository-level files or to a directory without a
`LICENSE`.

Every commit that is offered for inclusion must include a Signed-off-by trailer:

    feat: add new feature

    Signed-off-by: Your Name <your.email@example.com>

You can add it automatically:

    git commit -s -m "your commit message"

The sign-off is the certification in [DCO](DCO) and accepts [CLA](CLA) version
2.0 for that contribution. The project license grants the public the rights
for that project; the CLA separately grants the Project Owner the rights needed
to operate, sublicense, and relicense the contribution.

Only submit material that you own or are authorized to contribute. Disclose
all copied code, generated code, fonts, assets, data, patents, and third-party
license obligations in the pull request. If an employer, client, university,
or other organization owns any relevant right, an authorized representative of
that organization must accept the CLA before the contribution is submitted.

Projects may have additional technical contribution requirements.
